2026-09-23T07:02:21.7440980Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7441158Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7441385Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7441460Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7441572Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7441653Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7441750Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7441832Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7441940Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7442029Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7442118Z             return x + 1
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7442200Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7442282Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7442374Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7442477Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7442559Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7442634Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7442727Z     To execute it::
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7442808Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7442894Z         $ pytest
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7443052Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7443153Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7443236Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7443328Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7443412Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7443674Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7443855Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7443931Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7444029Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7444126Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7444217Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7444314Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7444497Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7444606Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7444767Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7444848Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7444927Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7445676Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7445757Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7445837Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7445920Z     Features
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7446007Z     --------
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7446085Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7446565Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7446640Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7446734Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7447035Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7447136Z       of test modules and functions
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7447218Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7447484Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7447655Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7447730Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7447997Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7448101Z       test suites out of the box
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7448176Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7448276Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7448359Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7448842Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
2026-09-23T07:02:21.7448917Z     
